+# EXEC001 STC SMT Cycles Offline License Issuer Guide
+
+This folder is the private issuer archive for the divergence / time-cycle project.
+Generated user folders must stay private and must not be committed.
+
+## Generate a license
+
+Run from the repository root:
+
+```bash
+python tools/stc_smt_deployment/offline_license_keygen.py \
+  --account 12345678 \
+  --server "Broker-ServerName" \
+  --expires 20261231 \
+  --first-name Amir \
+  --middle-name Hosein \
+  --last-name Heydar
+```
+
+For a server-independent license, use `--server-any` instead of `--server`:
+
+```bash
+python tools/stc_smt_deployment/offline_license_keygen.py \
+  --account 12345678 \
+  --server-any \
+  --expires 20261231 \
+  --first-name Amir \
+  --middle-name Hosein \
+  --last-name Heydar
+```
+
+The script prints and archives only the recipient-safe MT5 inputs:
+
+```text
+InpCycleModelProfile=<token>
+InpCycleOperatorMemo=<passphrase>
+InpCycleReferenceSeed=<gate 1>
+InpCycleDivergenceSeed=<gate 2>
+InpCycleExecutionSeed=<gate 3>
+InpCycleReleaseSeed=<gate 4>
+```
+
+## Archive format
+
+Default output folder:
+
+```text
+licenses/stc_smt_cycles/user0001-Amir-Hosein-Heydar/
+```
+
+Files per user:
+
+```text
+user0001-Amir-Hosein-Heydar_recipient_inputs.txt
+user0001-Amir-Hosein-Heydar_issuer_audit.json
+user0001-Amir-Hosein-Heydar_full_record.txt
+```
+
+Global index:
+
+```text
+licenses/stc_smt_cycles/issued_licenses_index.csv
+```
+
+## Runtime contract
+
+The protected EAs are fail-closed by default:
+
+- `mql5/Experts/IntermarketDivergenceExecution/IMDEXEC001_STC_SMT_Cycles.mq5`
+- `mql5/Experts/IntermarketDivergence/IMD001_CandleSessionDivergence.mq5`
+- `mql5/Experts/IntermarketDivergence/IMD001_SPX_NDX_TimeDivergence.mq5`
+
+They check:
+
+- product token prefix and product id: `STCSMT1` / `STCSMT`
+- MT5 account login
+- MT5 server hash, unless `--server-any` was used
+- expiry date
+- passphrase
+- four hidden gate values
+- offline signature match
+
+The license layer does not change the SMT, cycle, paper execution, real execution, partial close, hard close, drawing, or validation logic.
+It only allows or blocks runtime init/pulse.
